#: data/com.excelano.Comma.desktop.in:3
#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:6
msgid "Edit delimited text files"
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.desktop.in:10
msgid "CSV;TSV;DSV;Delimited;Table;Data;"
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:12
msgid ""
"Comma is a small editor for CSV, TSV, and other delimited text files. It "
"shows a file as a grid of values and saves it back as the same kind of file "
"it opened, leaving every row you did not edit byte for byte as it was."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:18
msgid ""
"Values are treated as text and never reinterpreted, so leading zeros "
"survive, long identifiers stay whole, and dates are whatever the file says "
"they are."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:23
msgid ""
"Comma is not a spreadsheet. There are no formulas, no cell formatting, and "
"no second file format to save into."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:32
msgid "David M. Anderson"
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:44
msgid ""
"Wide files draw faster. A file of forty-odd columns took about a second to "
"put its table on the screen and now takes around half of that, because the "
"height of a line of text is measured once for the whole grid rather than "
"again for every cell in it."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:50
msgid ""
"Building Comma from source now gives you an optimised binary. Asking Meson "
"for one had quietly been giving you the opposite."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:58
msgid ""
"The row numbers stay put when the grid is scrolled sideways, as the column "
"headings already did, so the number naming a row is beside it however far "
"across a wide file you have gone."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:63
msgid ""
"A row inserted mid-file no longer misnumbers the rows below it, and an edit "
"made to one of those rows is written to the row you typed into rather than "
"to the one above it."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:72
msgid ""
"Files open quickly. A cell now builds its editor when you type in it rather "
"than when the grid is drawn, so a file of four thousand rows opens in a "
"moment rather than in a couple of seconds, and a wide file gains the most."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:78
msgid ""
"Inserting or deleting a row redraws that row rather than the whole grid, so "
"the table stays where you had scrolled it to."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:86
msgid ""
"The first release. Comma opens a delimited file, guesses its delimiter and "
"says which one it guessed, and edits it as a grid. Rows and columns can be "
"inserted and deleted, everything can be undone, and saving a file changes "
"only the lines you edited."
msgstr ""

#: data/com.excelano.Comma.metainfo.xml.in:92
msgid ""
"Sorting and searching are views of the file rather than changes to it, and "
"one menu item writes a sort order down when you want it. What the grid is "
"showing can be exported as a PDF, a web page, or an OpenDocument spreadsheet."
msgstr ""

